{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bbmaj7]Who has be[Ebmaj7]lieved our mes[Bbmaj7]sage
And to [Ebmaj7]whom was the [Cm7]arm re[F7]vealed
[Ebmaj7]He grew like [F7]a root in [Bb]dry ground
No [Cm7]beauty to draw our eyes [F7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
De[Ebmaj7]spised and re[F7]jected by [Bbmaj7]men
A [Ebmaj7]man of [Cm7]sorrows [F7]and grief
[Ebmaj7]We hid [F7]our faces from [Bbmaj7]him
And [Cm7]held him [F7]of no ac[Bb]count
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Yet it was [Ebmaj7]our griefs he [F7]bore
Our [Dm7]sorrows he [Gm7]carried a[Cm7]lone [F7][Bb]
We thought him [Ebmaj7]struck by [F7]God
[Dm7]But pierced for our [Gm7]transgressions
[Cm7]Crushed for our iniquities
By his [F7]wounds we are [Bb]healed [Ebmaj7][F7]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]The punish[Ebmaj7]ment brought us [Bb]peace
Laid up[Ebmaj7]on him [Cm7]was the [F7]weight
[Ebmaj7]All we have [F7]strayed like [Bb]sheep
Turned to our own [Cm7]ways
The Lord laid on him
The in[F7]iquity of us all
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Yet it was our [Ebmaj7]griefs he [F7]bore
